) loops (vs c002)\",\"validation\":{\"correctness_reasoning\":\"conv/GN math unchanged; only removed suspect trace-time constructs\",\"all_workloads_pass\":false,\"passed\":0,\"total\":5},\"per_workload\":[{\"uuid\":\"952fec71-f323-5dab-9340-dad59ad7a3f1\",\"B\":4,\"H\":256,\"W\":256,\"status\":\"RUNTIME_ERROR\",\"pass\":false,\"speedup\":null,\"max_abs\":0.0,\"max_rel\":0.0},{\"uuid\":\"6284bbd2-bc2e-5002-856a-c4f2c7582254\",\"B\":32,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"RUNTIME_ERROR\",\"pass\":false,\"speedup\":null,\"max_abs\":0.0,\"max_rel\":0.0},{\"uuid\":\"a4c930bb-4694-570b-8d51-97ba053f74ac\",\"B\":1,\"H\":128,\"W\":128,\"status\":\"RUNTIME_ERROR\",\"pass\":false,\"speedup\":null,\"max_abs\":0.0,\"max_rel\":0.0},{\"uuid\":\"144fdf2b-0296-5d64-819b-eab16d18c752\",\"B\":64,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"RUNTIME_ERROR\",\"pass\":false,\"speedup\":null,\"max_abs\":0.0,\"max_rel\":0.0},{\"uuid\":\"8de1dc63-b34a-5618-ba36-abaa79de54cf\",\"B\":1,\"H\":768,\"W\":768,\"status\":\"RUNTIME_ERROR\",\"pass\":false,\"speedup\":null,\"max_abs\":0.0,\"max_rel\":0.0}],\"geomean_speedup\":null,\"decision\":\"invalid; identical uniform RUNTIME_ERROR (all 5, max_abs=max_rel=0.0). REFUTES the input_precision-kwarg hypothesis. Since the failure poisons the very first (conv) kernel's output, the fault must be a trace-time construct unique to the conv kernel. Remaining suspect: capture of the module-global Python int _KS inside the @triton.jit conv body. Next: c004 makes kernel-size a tl.constexpr param and removes all module-global capture from the conv kernel, branching from c003.\",\"cumulative_evaluations\":3,\"skill_usage\":{\"KernelWiki\":\"not used (Blackwell/Hopper-only; target is Ampere sm_80)\"}}\n{\"candidate_id\":\"c004\",\"parent\":\"c003\",\"source_sha256\":\"2e09a6be1f625b22ecf741f67eade6b826bf0fb5c1c9a8e0790b4c7d32f3a41b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-18T00:00:00+08:00\",\"hypothesis\":\"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is trace-time capture of the module-global Python int _KS inside the @triton.jit conv body. Passing kernel-size as a tl.constexpr param KS and removing ALL module-global capture from the conv kernel fixes it; fp32 tl.dot (native TF32 on sm_80) then produces correct output within atol because GroupNorm absorbs the ~5e-4 relative conv error.\",\"lever\":\"make kernel-size a tl.constexpr param KS; remove all module-global (_KS) capture from conv jit body (vs c003)\",\"validation\":{\"correctness_reasoning\":\"conv indexing/padding, GroupNorm grouping (32 groups x 8ch), biased variance, per-channel affine, SiLU, residual = original x — all re-verified vs plan §2; evaluator confirms 5/5 pass within atol\",\"all_workloads_pass\":true,\"passed\":5,\"total\":5},\"per_workload\":[{\"uuid\":\"952fec71-f323-5dab-9340-dad59ad7a3f1\",\"B\":4,\"H\":256,\"W\":256,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":8.211598,\"sol_ms\":55.271973,\"speedup\":0.1486},{\"uuid\":\"6284bbd2-bc2e-5002-856a-c4f2c7582254\",\"B\":32,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":3.803132,\"sol_ms\":27.023950,\"speedup\":0.1407},{\"uuid\":\"a4c930bb-4694-570b-8d51-97ba053f74ac\",\"B\":1,\"H\":128,\"W\":128,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":0.757605,\"sol_ms\":3.898732,\"speedup\":0.1943},{\"uuid\":\"144fdf2b-0296-5d64-819b-eab16d18c752\",\"B\":64,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":7.572300,\"sol_ms\":54.581815,\"speedup\":0.1387},{\"uuid\":\"8de1dc63-b34a-5618-ba36-abaa79de54cf\",\"B\":1,\"H\":768,\"W\":768,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":25.701636,\"sol_ms\":133.995995,\"speedup\":0.1918}],\"geomean_speedup\":0.1610,\"arithmetic_mean_speedup\":0.1628,\"decision\":\"keep as new best-parent (first VALID candidate; correctness anchor). Root cause of c001-c003 uniform faults CONFIRMED = module-global _KS capture in the jitted conv, now eliminated. Geomean 0.1610x (<1.0) as expected for a naive un-tuned implicit-GEMM conv vs cuDNN. Small-batch/large-spatial shapes (WL3 0.194x, WL5 0.192x) fare best; large-batch small-spatial (WL2 0.141x, WL4 0.139x) worst — conv heavily under-utilizes tensor cores. Next: c005 introduces conv autotune (BLOCK_M/N/K, num_warps, num_stages) to raise tensor-core utilization.\",\"best_candidate_id\":\"c004\",\"cumulative_evaluations\":4,\"skill_usage\":{\"KernelWiki\":\"not used (Blackwell/Hopper-only; target is Ampere sm_80)\"}}\n{\"candidate_id\":\"c005\",\"parent\":\"c004\",\"source_sha256\":\"0ad34bdcb116b76591727a6f60dc0d4381d5f534e3b8af57879ff355854a5ddd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-18T00:00:00+08:00\",\"hypothesis\":\"c004's fixed conservative conv tile (BLOCK_M=N=K=64, warps=4, stages=2) under-utilizes Ampere TF32 tensor cores; adding @triton.autotune over larger (BLOCK_M,BLOCK_N,BLOCK_K,num_warps,num_stages) configs keyed on (M,C,H,W) should raise MMA occupancy and speed up the conv, most on the currently-worst large-batch/small-spatial WL2/WL4.\",\"lever\":\"wrap _conv3x3_kernel in @triton.autotune (11 configs, key=[M,C,H,W]); grid uses meta[BLOCK_M/N]; all conv/GN math byte-identical to c004\",\"validation\":{\"correctness_reasoning\":\"only tiling/scheduling changed; BLOCK_K in {64,128,256} always divides C=256 (no channel over-read); BLOCK_M/N fully masked by m_mask/n_mask so any tile is safe on all shapes; oversized configs pruned by autotuner (OutOfResources skipped). Evaluator confirms 5/5 pass within atol.\",\"all_workloads_pass\":true,\"passed\":5,\"total\":5},\"per_workload\":[{\"uuid\":\"952fec71-f323-5dab-9340-dad59ad7a3f1\",\"B\":4,\"H\":256,\"W\":256,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":8.211598,\"sol_ms\":20.246372,\"speedup\":0.4056},{\"uuid\":\"6284bbd2-bc2e-5002-856a-c4f2c7582254\",\"B\":32,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":3.803132,\"sol_ms\":9.962343,\"speedup\":0.3818},{\"uuid\":\"a4c930bb-4694-570b-8d51-97ba053f74ac\",\"B\":1,\"H\":128,\"W\":128,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":0.757605,\"sol_ms\":1.688329,\"speedup\":0.4487},{\"uuid\":\"144fdf2b-0296-5d64-819b-eab16d18c752\",\"B\":64,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":7.572300,\"sol_ms\":19.550075,\"speedup\":0.3873},{\"uuid\":\"8de1dc63-b34a-5618-ba36-abaa79de54cf\",\"B\":1,\"H\":768,\"W\":768,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":25.701636,\"sol_ms\":53.991194,\"speedup\":0.4760}],\"geomean_speedup\":0.4183,\"arithmetic_mean_speedup\":0.4199,\"decision\":\"keep as new best-parent. Conv autotune lifted geomean 0.1610x->0.4183x (+160%), uniformly across all 5 workloads (WL1 0.149->0.406, WL2 0.141->0.382, WL3 0.194->0.449, WL4 0.139->0.387, WL5 0.192->0.476). Confirms the c004 conv was tensor-core-throughput-bound. Still <1.0 vs cuDNN. Next lever (c006): reduce per-tap global-memory traffic in the conv — the current impl re-loads the input for all 9 taps and reads weights strided; try weight prepermute to tap-contiguous [kh,kw,cin,cout] layout so W tiles are contiguous, branching from c005.\",\"best_candidate_id\":\"c005\",\"cumulative_evaluations\":5,\"skill_usage\":{\"KernelWiki\":\"not used (Blackwell/Hopper-only; target is Ampere sm_80)\"}}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"candidate_id\":\"c003\",\"parent\":\"c002\",\"source_sha256\":\"6edc918463e36ea8a35b54bf3b810833b25d23256e503c1643c3d24ba9be1217\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-18T00:00:00+08:00\",\"hypothesis\":\"The uniform precision-independent RUNTIME_ERROR in c001/c002 is a trace-time fault from the tl.dot(input_precision=) kwarg (unsupported on the installed Triton, which used allow_tf32=). Remove the kwarg (fp32 tl.dot defaults to TF32 tensor cores on sm_80); also pass host-side inv_group_size instead of group_size.to(float) and use plain range() loops.\",\"lever\":\"remove input_precision= kwarg from tl.dot; host-side inv_group_size; plain range() loops (vs c002)\",\"validation\":{\"correctness_reasoning\":\"conv/GN math unchanged; only removed suspect trace-time constructs\",\"all_workloads_pass\":false,\"passed\":0,\"total\":5},\"per_wo