ion.\",\"best_candidate_id\":\"c004\",\"cumulative_evaluations\":4,\"skill_usage\":{\"KernelWiki\":\"not used (Blackwell/Hopper-only; target is Ampere sm_80)\"}}"," {\"candidate_id\":\"c005\",\"parent\":\"c004\",\"source_sha256\":\"0ad34bdcb116b76591727a6f60dc0d4381d5f534e3b8af57879ff355854a5ddd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-18T00:00:00+08:00\",\"hypothesis\":\"c004's fixed conservative conv tile (BLOCK_M=N=K=64, warps=4, stages=2) under-utilizes Ampere TF32 tensor cores; adding @triton.autotune over larger (BLOCK_M,BLOCK_N,BLOCK_K,num_warps,num_stages) configs keyed on (M,C,H,W) should raise MMA occupancy and speed up the conv, most on the currently-worst large-batch/small-spatial WL2/WL4.\",\"lever\":\"wrap _conv3x3_kernel in @triton.autotune (11 configs, key=[M,C,H,W]); grid uses meta[BLOCK_M/N]; all conv/GN math byte-identical to c004\",\"validation\":{\"correctness_reasoning\":\"only tiling/scheduling changed; BLOCK_K in {64,128,256} always divides C=256 (no channel over-read); BLOCK_M/N fully masked by m_mask/n_mask so any tile is safe on all shapes; oversized configs pruned by autotuner (OutOfResources skipped). Evaluator confirms 5/5 pass within atol.\",\"all_workloads_pass\":true,\"passed\":5,\"total\":5},\"per_workload\":[{\"uuid\":\"952fec71-f323-5dab-9340-dad59ad7a3f1\",\"B\":4,\"H\":256,\"W\":256,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":8.211598,\"sol_ms\":20.246372,\"speedup\":0.4056},{\"uuid\":\"6284bbd2-bc2e-5002-856a-c4f2c7582254\",\"B\":32,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":3.803132,\"sol_ms\":9.962343,\"speedup\":0.3818},{\"uuid\":\"a4c930bb-4694-570b-8d51-97ba053f74ac\",\"B\":1,\"H\":128,\"W\":128,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":0.757605,\"sol_ms\":1.688329,\"speedup\":0.4487},{\"uuid\":\"144fdf2b-0296-5d64-819b-eab16d18c752\",\"B\":64,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":7.572300,\"sol_ms\":19.550075,\"speedup\":0.3873},{\"uuid\":\"8de1dc63-b34a-5618-ba36-abaa79de54cf\",\"B\":1,\"H\":768,\"W\":768,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":25.701636,\"sol_ms\":53.991194,\"speedup\":0.4760}],\"geomean_speedup\":0.4183,\"arithmetic_mean_speedup\":0.4199,\"decision\":\"keep as new best-parent. Conv autotune lifted geomean 0.1610x->0.4183x (+160%), uniformly across all 5 workloads (WL1 0.149->0.406, WL2 0.141->0.382, WL3 0.194->0.449, WL4 0.139->0.387, WL5 0.192->0.476). Confirms the c004 conv was tensor-core-throughput-bound. Still <1.0 vs cuDNN. Next lever (c006): reduce per-tap global-memory traffic in the conv — the current impl re-loads the input for all 9 taps and reads weights strided; try weight prepermute to tap-contiguous [kh,kw,cin,cout] layout so W tiles are contiguous, branching from c005.\",\"best_candidate_id\":\"c005\",\"cumulative_evaluations\":5,\"skill_usage\":{\"KernelWiki\":\"not used (Blackwell/Hopper-only; target is Ampere sm_80)\"}}","+{\"candidate_id\":\"c006\",\"parent\":\"c005\",\"source_sha256\":\"47467c373bc14ddd8c6f8ea97906580aea6fea728a93932f73347de1a09a3b53\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-18T00:00:00+08:00\",\"hypothesis\":\"c005's conv loads the weight W-tile from native (Cout,Cin,3,3) layout with cout strided by C*KK=2304 and cin by KK=9 (fully uncoalesced), re-read from L2 for every M-tile. A one-time Triton permute of each conv weight to tap-contiguous [KK,Cin,Cout] (cout stride-1) makes the W-tile coalesced and the tl.dot B-operand natural row-major, cutting L2 weight traffic and improving conv throughput.\",\"lever\":\"one-time Triton weight permute (Cout,Cin,3,3)->[KK,Cin,Cout]; conv reads permuted weight with cout contiguous (vs c005). Conv autotune configs + all other kernels byte-identical.\",\"validation\":{\"correctness_reasoning\":\"permute is a pure index remap dst[tap,cin,cout]<-src[cout,cin,tap]; conv still contracts weight[cout,cin,kh,kw] against same input pixels, only operand storage order changed. BLOCK_K in {64,128,256} divides C=256 (cin unmasked ok); BLOCK_N masked by n_mask. Evaluator confirms 5/5 pass within atol.\",\"all_workloads_pass\":true,\"passed\":5,\"total\":5},\"per_workload\":[{\"uuid\":\"952fec71-f323-5dab-9340-dad59ad7a3f1\",\"B\":4,\"H\":256,\"W\":256,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":8.211598,\"sol_ms\":10.142410,\"speedup\":0.8096},{\"uuid\":\"6284bbd2-bc2e-5002-856a-c4f2c7582254\",\"B\":32,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":3.803132,\"sol_ms\":4.783468,\"speedup\":0.7951},{\"uuid\":\"a4c930bb-4694-570b-8d51-97ba053f74ac\",\"B\":1,\"H\":128,\"W\":128,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":0.757605,\"sol_ms\":1.071229,\"speedup\":0.7072},{\"uuid\":\"144fdf2b-0296-5d64-819b-eab16d18c752\",\"B\":64,\"H\":64,\"W\":64,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":7.572300,\"sol_ms\":9.131698,\"speedup\":0.8292},{\"uuid\":\"8de1dc63-b34a-5618-ba36-abaa79de54cf\",\"B\":1,\"H\":768,\"W\":768,\"status\":\"OK\",\"pass\":true,\"ref_ms\":25.701636,\"sol_ms\":32.398065,\"speedup\":0.7933}],\"geomean_speedup\":0.7857,\"arithmetic_mean_speedup\":0.7869,\"decision\":\"keep as new best-parent. Weight prepermute lifted geomean 0.4183x->0.7857x (+88%), uniformly (WL1 0.406->0.810, WL2 0.382->0.795, WL3 0.449->0.707, WL4 0.387->0.829, WL5 0.192->... WL5 0.476->0.793). Confirms the c005 conv was heavily L2/weight-load-bound. Approaching parity with cuDNN (best WL4 0.829x). Next lever (c007): cut elementwise/reduction memory passes vs the reference by fusing GN-apply+SiLU into the next conv's input load OR fusing GN stats into conv epilogue; alternatively cache input tiles across the 9 taps in the conv to remove redundant input re-loads. Choose the input-reload fix first (largest remaining conv traffic).\",\"best_candidate_id\":\"c006\",\"cumulative_evaluations\":6,\"skill_usage\":{\"KernelWiki\":\"not used (Blackwell/Hopper-only; target is Ampere sm_80)\"}}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2f8acb2f-14ce-4702-a319-a2253f6f9745","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MybncXnPNgiKjnXqCmRVBc","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L1-002_vae_conv3x3_groupnorm_silu_residual_fused/docs/plan.md","old_string":"### c006 plan (next turn) — one lever\n- **Lever:** **weight prepermute**. The conv currently reads weights with the strided access `w[co, ci, kh, kw]` (stride `KK=9` in `ci`, non-contiguous W tiles). Add a one-time Triton kernel that permutes each `conv{1,2}_weight` from `(Cout,Cin,3,3)` to tap-contiguous `(kh,kw,Cin,Cout)`, so each tap's W tile `[cin, cout]` is fully contiguous → coalesced weight loads and a cleaner `tl.dot` operand. Weights are tiny (2.4 MB) so the permute cost is negligible and reused across all M-tiles. The conv kernel's weight-pointer math changes to index the permuted layout; conv output math is identical. Hypothesis: coalesced weight loads improve conv throughput, most on the large workloads. Risk: permute indexing bug (correctness) — re-verify the (kh,kw,cin,cout) mapping against §2.\n- **Alternative if c006 disappoints:** the conv re-loads the full input for all 9 taps; consider caching input tiles in SRAM across taps (restructure the tap loop inside the K loop), or an NHWC layout transform (draft §5.2) so input `[pixel,cin]` tiles are contiguous.","new_string":"### c006 plan (next turn) — one lever\n- **Lever:** **weight prepermute**. The conv currently reads weights with the strided access `w[co, ci, kh, kw]` (stride `KK=9` in `ci`, non-contiguous W tiles). Add a one-time Triton kernel that permutes each `conv{1,2}_weight` from `(Cout,Cin,3,3)` to tap-contiguous `(kh,kw,Cin,Cout)`, so each tap's W tile `[cin, cout]` is fully contiguous → coalesced weight loads and a cleaner `tl.dot` operand. Weights are tiny (2.4 MB) so the permute cost is negligible and reused across all M-tiles. The conv kernel's weight-pointer math changes to index the permuted layout; conv output math is identical. Hypothesis: coalesced weight loads improve conv throughput, most on the large workloads. Risk: permute indexing bug (correctness) — re-verify the (kh,kw,cin,cout) mapping against §2.\n- **Alternative if c006 disappoints:** the conv re-loads the full input for all 9 taps; consider caching input tiles in SRAM across taps (restructure the tap loop inside the K loop), or an NHWC layout transform (draft §5.2) so input `[pixel,cin]` tiles are contiguous.\n\n### c006 (weight prepermute) — VALID ✅ new best\n- Single lever vs c005: one-time Triton permute of each conv weight `(Cout,Cin,3,3)`→`[KK,Cin,Cout]` (cout stride-1); conv reads permuted weight with coalesced W-tile. Autotune configs + all other kernels byte-identical.\n- Result: **5/5 PASS**. Geomean **0.7857x** (up from c005 0.4183x, **+88%**), arithmetic 0.7869x. `cumulative_evaluations = 6`.\n  - Per-workload: WL1 0.406→0.810, WL2 0.382→0.795, WL3 0.449→0.707, WL4 0.387→0.829, WL5 0.476→0.793. Uniform lift → the c005 conv was heavily L2/weight-load-bound.\n- **Decision:** keep as best-parent (`best_candidate_id=c006`, `best_geomean=0.7857`). Now approaching cuDNN parity (best WL4 0.829x). Conv weight traffic largely solved; remaining conv inefficiency is redundant **input** re-loads (input reloaded for all 9 taps).\n\n### c007 plan (next turn) — one lever\n- **Lever:** **cut redundant conv input traffic / elementwise passes.** Two candidate mechanisms, pick the one with the larger expected remaining win:\n  1. **Input reuse across taps in the conv.** Currently the 3×3 tap loop reloads overlapping input rows 9× from L2. Restructure so the input is loaded once per (M-tile, cin-tile) and reused for the applicable taps (shift within SRAM), or move the K(cin) loop outermost with the 9 taps sharing a cached input panel. Reduces conv input L2 traffic ~9×→~1× on the reused region.\n  2. **Fuse GN-apply+SiLU into conv2's input load** (read raw `t1`, apply normalize·affine·silu on-the-fly using precomputed stats; drop `t2` materialization) — saves a full write+read of a 256-ch map. Trade-off: activation recomputed ~9× (draft §5.5.1); may not pay in a compute-bound conv.\n- Start with mechanism (1) if the conv is still the dominant cost (it is — conv >> elementwise). Keep exactly one mechanism per candidate id; branch from c006. Watch that restructuring preserves masking/correctness.\n- **Note on convergence:** we have gone 0.1610→0.4183→0.7857. Each conv lever has paid off strongly; continue while conv gains remain, then harvest fusion (GN/SiLU/residual pass reduction). Converge when consecutive VALID candidates improve geomean <2% and remaining levers are exhausted (plan §6)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":99675,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33a0ba3d-9c2f-4372-a092-6f22171b558e","uuid":"12771b1b-fbca-4798-94ac-13bd02071892","timestamp":"2026-09-18T00:01:34.010Z"}
